Z||000004||jerpro||12-02-2000||03:56 PM||||Don't you dare!!!!!!!<BR>GM put the sway bar there for a reason. If you want to imrove handling buy the front/rear kit.<BR>I would hate seeing a fiero enthusiast get killed because he thought he was smarter than GM.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>If you need more info check this web page: <A HREF="http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/Cornering.html" TARGET=_blank> <A HREF="http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/Cornering.html</A>" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/Cornering.html[/URL]</A>  <BR>and <A HREF="http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/dynamics102.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/dynamics102.html</A> <BR>please don't drive your fiero without sway bars!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Only try your best, and if you don't succeed... TRY HARDER.<p>[This message has been edited by jerpro (edited 12-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||gixxer||12-02-2000||04:32 PM||||Big F, I see your reasoning and it is at least, partly correct. One of the reasons for having a swaybar, or having a larger diameter bar, is to degrade the traction at that end of the car. This matches the traction at one end of the car to the other end, hopefully resulting in neutral handling or slight understeer. <BR>However, removing the front(and only) bar will lead to some secondary consequences.<BR>*There will probably not be enough roll resistance with the stock springs to prevent the car from bottoming the suspension over bumps in turns.<BR>*The car will probably roll far enough that it will HURT traction front and/or rear by allowing the suspension to put the tires into unfavorable camber angles.<BR>*The car will probably have an unsettled rolling or swaying motion at speed.<BR>*Exiting a slow corner under power, the inside rear wheel will lift and unload(because the ouside front is compressed), causing wheelspin. <BR>*The car will tend to oversteer, then with a bad steering wheel correction will tend to snap back in the other direction causing you to back it into a lamppost =0..<BR>However, the ride will be better...<P>   ||||reg||1
